    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Crowley are delighted to bring to the market this exceptionally well located derelict house, offering stunning sea views in a truly beautiful waterfront setting.\n \nLocated in the sought-after area of Rosmoney, Rosmeena Lodge is just footsteps from a charming jetty and only a one-minute walk from Rosmoney Pier, where sailing boats are moored on the water. Home to the Mayo Sailing Club, the pier and surrounding area have a lovely, picturesque feel, with boats coming and going across the bay.\n\nThe derelict house sits on a site extending to approximately 0.12 ha/0.3 acres with a certified septic tank and mains water available to the site. We believe the property will qualify for the derelict homes grant, giving a purchaser an excellent opportunity to restore/build to their own requirements.\n \nThe residence is located in Rosmoney, one of Westport's most popular areas, and is just a 12 minute drive from Westport town and all its facilities. There are the added benefits of being close to a wide choice of amenities including Carrowholly National School, Westport Golf Course, rugby and football clubs. Rosmoney Pier, the home of Mayo Sailing Club, is just 100 metres from the property.\n\nSpecial Features\n• Exceptional sea views & waterfront setting\n• Approx. 0.3 acre site\n• Derelict house with renovation potential\n• Potential eligibility for Derelict Homes Grant\n• 100m from Rosmoney Pier\n• 10 minute drive to Westport\n\nDirections\nFrom Westport take the Newport road for 0.9 km and turn left onto Golf Course Road, continue on for approximately 5 km and turn right at sign for Rosmoney (shortly after passing Carrowholly Primary School), after 1 km turn left, continue towards Rosmoney for 1.5 km and the property is on the left"
      },
